  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Wall to wall – turn and carry it over the line",
  "description": "Four cones make a box of about 5 × 5 metres. Two players meet 1v1 inside the box, and each has their own goal line – an imaginary line between two of the cones. Whoever has the puck tries to turn away from the opponent and skate with the puck over their line. If the opponent wins the puck, they attack their own line instead.\n\nPlay about a minute at a time and change opponents if a game is uneven. Set up several boxes side by side so everyone plays at once. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Turn with your body between the opponent and the puck."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "What is your favourite way to turn with the puck?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defender: when is it hardest to take the puck from someone turning?"
    }
  ],
